  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We profiled 64 bulk RNA-seq samples of human airway epithelium and have a TF motif prior and a STRING protein interaction table. I'd like PANDA to build the TF-to-gene network and then CONDOR to break it into modules of regulators and their targets."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"PANDA to build the TF-to-gene network\" -- available from PANDA.\n2. \"CONDOR to break it into modules of regulators and their targets\" -- available from CONDOR.\n\nYour request has 2 steps, one after the other: each step uses the result of the one before. Each step is listed with the registered workflows that fit it, their algorithmic premises and inputs:\n\n**Step 1 -- \"TF-to-gene network\"**\nResult: regulatory networks, from expression matrix.\n- TF-only regulatory network:\n  - **PANDA** — Message passing iteratively reconciles a regulator-target prior with other biological evidence networks. Per-sample version: **LIONESS-PANDA**. Needs expression matrix, motif/prior and PPI network.\n  - **OTTER** — OTTER optimizes a TF-gene matrix W so that W W-transpose matches the TF-TF interaction network and W-transpose W matches gene co-expression. Needs motif/prior, PPI network and either expression matrix or adjusted co-expression matrix.\n- TF-only signed regulatory-effect network:\n  - **GIRAFFE** — GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality. Needs expression matrix, motif/prior and PPI network.\n\n**Step 2 -- \"modules of regulators and their targets\"**\nResult: community assignments (aggregate), from the regulatory networks of the previous step.\nNo single registered workflow produces this from the stated inputs; a registered handoff does, in two steps:\n- **PANDA → CONDOR** — PANDA infers a regulatory network from the expression matrix; CONDOR then takes that network and returns its communities (modules).\n- **OTTER → CONDOR** — OTTER infers a regulatory network from the expression matrix; CONDOR then takes that network and returns its communities (modules).\n  - Method premise: find communities in a two-mode network; return network modules or community membership\n\nShould we start with step 1 (PANDA or LIONESS-PANDA or OTTER or GIRAFFE)? Each step is planned and approved on its own. Step 2 has no registered workflow; what to do instead is described above.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
